  "id": "magnetic-resonance-imaging",
  "term": "magnetic resonance imaging",
  "definition": "Magnetic resonance imaging is a non-invasive brain imaging method used to study brain structure, function, and white-matter pathways. In developmental research, it is used to examine how prenatal exposures may affect the developing brain and how early brain findings relate to later infant outcomes.",
